      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Systemic racism in housing and banking often operates through historical policies like redlining, which explicitly denied certain neighborhoods credit and investment, leading to long-term disinvestment and segregation. Modern manifestations include zoning laws that restrict multi-family housing and implicit bias in lending algorithms that disproportionately favor white applicants. To effectively teach this, guide high schoolers in analyzing current real estate data to reveal patterns of exclusion and practice ethical argumentation about equity. This project supports your curriculum by moving beyond abstract concepts to concrete evidence of how policy and practice reinforce inequality.",
