      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so, if i'm setting up the lesson, is it actually accurate to say that these 'individual choice' arguments are essentially just being used to mask systemic issues? like, is there a consensus in the sociology field that these arguments aren't actually based on real economic data, but are just ways to avoid talking about race?",
